# ARD build artefacts and local secrets.
#
# Credentials live outside the repository on purpose: a secret inside the tree is
# one `git add -A` away from being published, and .gitignore is not a security
# boundary -- it does not apply to files that are already tracked, and history
# keeps copies of anything that was ever committed.

# Compiled binaries. Every one that `go build ./...` can produce at the repository root is
# listed, so that a stray `go build -o ard-connect .` does not become a committed artefact.
/ard-agent
/ard-server
/ard-ca
/ard-connect
/ardctl
/probe
/mockadbd
/bin/
/dist/

# Locally built binaries, including the ones the end-to-end script compiles.
/.e2e-bin/

# Key material. Certificates are excluded too: a public .crt is not a secret, but
# nothing in this repository needs one committed, and a PKI directory that is
# half-committed is worse than one that is entirely absent.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.jks
*.keystore
/android/build/
/android/*.jks
/android/ard-agent.apk
/android/ard-agent.apk.idsig

# Editor and OS noise.
*.swp
.DS_Store